    "rationale": "Plectin is a cytoskeletal linker expressed in skin and muscle. Biallelic PLEC variants can cause EBS with generalized blistering followed by progressive muscular dystrophy. The cleavage plane within basal keratinocytes just above hemidesmosomes supports an EBS-level defect. Strongest alternative resolved: Basal-keratinocyte cleavage plus progressive muscular dystrophy is the syndromic PLEC-EBS pattern; the distractors do not unify that cleavage level and myopathy."
